.TH CARGO-CHECKUP 1 "2026-09-27" "cargo-checkup 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cargo-checkup \- unified cargo health check for Rust workspaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cargo checkup
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B cargo-checkup init
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B cargo-checkup completions
\fISHELL\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs unused, outdated, duplicate, advisory, license, banned and hygiene
checks over a Cargo workspace in one pass, prints a unified report and
optionally applies fixes.
Exit code 1 when a warn/error finding exists (or matches \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR),
0 when clean or info-only, 2 on tool errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to Cargo.toml (defaults to current dir).
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIhuman|json|sarif\fR
Output format (default: human). sarif fits GitHub code scanning.
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Skip network checks (outdated, advisory).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
Ignore the disk cache for crates.io lookups.
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\-unused\fR
Also flag optional dependencies that look unused.
.TP
\fB\-\-fix\fR
Apply all auto-fixes and exit 0 on success.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Print what \fB\-\-fix\fR would do without changing anything.
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fILIST\fR
Only run these checks (comma-separated).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fILIST\fR
Skip these checks (comma-separated).
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fILIST\fR
Fail only on these checks (comma-separated).
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to checkup.toml policy file (auto-discovered by default).
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\fR \fIPATH\fR
Suppress findings recorded in the baseline file.
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\-update\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write current findings as the new baseline file.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fIcheckup.toml\fR
Policy file in the workspace root: [licenses], [banned], [msrv], [fix],
[[ignore]] rules.
.SH EXAMPLES
cargo checkup --offline
.br
cargo checkup --format sarif > results.sarif
.br
cargo checkup --baseline-update .checkup-baseline.json
.br
cargo checkup --fix
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cargo(1)
